## 🚀 Overview

This project presents a hardware-accelerated image enhancement pipeline using Residual Convolutional Neural Networks (Residual CNNs) deployed on FPGA hardware using Vitis AI.

The system is optimized for:

* ⚡ Real-time FPGA inference
* 🧠 Edge AI deployment
* 🌙 Low-light enhancement
* 🧹 Noise reduction
* 🔍 Blur restoration
* 📦 Efficient INT8 quantized execution

The deployment pipeline integrates deep learning optimization with FPGA-oriented hardware acceleration for low-power, high-throughput inference.

---

## ✨ Key Features

* Residual CNN image enhancement architecture
* INT8 Quantization-Aware Training (QAT)
* FPGA DPU deployment workflow
* Vitis AI integration
* Docker-based reproducible environment
* FPGA inference benchmarking
* PSNR / SSIM evaluation
* Hardware-software co-design
* `.xmodel` FPGA deployment support
* Real-time edge inference pipeline

---

## 🧠 System Architecture

```text
Dataset
   ↓
Residual CNN Training
   ↓
Quantization-Aware Training
   ↓
INT8 Optimization
   ↓
Vitis AI Compilation
   ↓
XModel Generation
   ↓
DPU Deployment
   ↓
FPGA Inference
   ↓
Enhanced Output
```

---

## ⚡ Performance

| Metric          | CPU (FP32)     | FPGA (INT8) |
| --------------- | -------------- | ----------- |
| Inference Speed | 0.85 – 1.3 FPS | 8.37 FPS    |
| Precision       | FP32           | INT8        |
| Speedup         | 1×             | 8–10×       |
| Deployment      | CPU            | FPGA DPU    |
| Optimization    | None           | Quantized   |

---

## 📊 Evaluation Metrics

The project evaluates enhancement quality using:

* PSNR (Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio)
* SSIM (Structural Similarity Index)

The FPGA deployment maintains strong visual quality while achieving significantly faster inference.

